[Music]  coti de pablo may be known for ncis but  did you know she co-hosted a television  series at 15. keep watching to find out  how dipablo transformed into the artist  people know and love today  born maria jose de pablo fernandez in  santiago chile de pablo moved with her  family to miami florida after her mother  was hired as a talk show host at the  spanish language television network  telemundo while acclimating to her new  surroundings other kids had trouble  pronouncing maria jose so de pablo told  them to call her koti a traditional  nickname for her given name as a child  de pablo developed a love of music and  entertainment but her drive for the arts  didn't really start until she attended  an elective drama class in middle school  speaking with carnegie mellon today in a  2010 interview di pablo reminisced about  a pivotal moment during this class  saying i remember i was on stage in a  scene and something happened and i  called somebody  my teacher took me off stage gave me  detention i said to myself there's  something very wrong with this class i  knew i just needed to find the proper  class after middle school de pablo  attended new world school of the arts  pursuing her newfound passion at 15  years old dipablo worked as a co-host  for the latin american talk show control  from 1994 to 1995. she hosted episodes  alongside carlos ponce who was at the  time a rising star in latin american  telenovelas  after high school de pablo was driven to  continue her formal acting education she  told carnegie mellon today of how she  knew that carnegie mellon university  known for its fantastic music theater  program was the right place for her  recalling i always felt like they  understood me i was pretty complex i was  an immigrant and my family was very far  away i was both incredibly fragile and  incredibly strong and i think they could  see that and i will always be grateful  for that while at cmu de pablo  participated in many notable university  musicals which included and the world  goes round the fantastics the running  musical in history and the late great  stephen sondheim's 1973 musical a little  night music upon graduating in 2000 with  a bachelor of fine arts and musical  theater de pablo joined the ranks of  other famous actors who've made it  through carnegie mellon university this  list includes the likes of ted danson  holly hunter renee elise goldsberry and  ethan hawk  after college de pablo determined her  best move was to relocate to new york  city and start auditioning for roles so  she did exactly that in a 2007 interview  with the jewish journal de pablo spoke  about working as a waitress in manhattan  and brooklyn to pay the bills while  performing in william shakespeare's  measure for measure at the new york city  public theater her first screen  appearance came in a volkswagen  commercial which was succeeded by minor  work and single episodes of the  television series the street and the  education of max bickford as well as a  voice role in the 2002 racing video game  toca race driver yeah  maybe later on you could take me out for  you hey you cut this crap and get the  hell up there during this time de  pablo's passion for music was also  thriving and she snagged a supporting  role in the stage adaptation of the 1992  academy award-nominated feature film the  mambo kings which was based on the 1989  pulitzer prize-winning novel the mambo  kings play songs of love by oscar e  huelos while the musical's trial run in  san francisco was staged with the hope  that it would soon move to broadway poor  reviews canceled any further production  plans de pablo subsequently would star  in the only season of the 2004 law drama  the jury in which she played her first  major recurring role  while de pablo was working on the mambo  kings she submitted a videotape audition  for the role of special agent david for  ncis a series at the time known mainly  as a growing spin-off of the popular  television series jag after sending in  her tape de pablo was called into los  angeles for a screen test with michael  weatherly one of her future ncis  co-stars what are you saying  she's saying you're a car killer  what a car killer everybody needs a  hobby in an interview with tv fanatic in  2009 de pablo spoke about her experience  when weatherly decided to start  improvising i just thought oh my god  this guy is sabotaging my audition i  will not allow this actor to do this to  me so what people saw in the audition  room really was a person fighting the  other person back and refusing to give  even an inch it was just all the things  that i think later on translated to the  relationship that ziva and tony had and  still have despite throwing to pablo off  her game weatherly's move and the  pablo's response seemed to work as the  actress was offered the part de pablo's  character of mossad agent ziva david  filled the spot left by sasha  alexander's special agent kate todd  who's brutally killed in the season 2  finale of ncis originally designed to be  european the writers and producers of  ncis changed david's backstory to be  israeli de pablo put a lot of effort  throughout her time on ncis into making  her character feel as authentic as  possible despite the fact that the  actress isn't jewish herself she learned  how to speak hebrew realistically very  early on and de pablo went even further  studying the history of jewish  civilization and culture her devotion to  her performance has kept david a fan  favorite character and has netted to  pablo numerous award nominations and an  alma award in 2011 for outstanding  actress in a drama television series  after eight seasons on ncis de pablo  decided to leave the show cbs claimed to  have offered de pablo a considerable  contract to entice her to stay but she  explained in a 2016 q a which was quoted  in a 2019 article by vanity fair  i worked eight years crafting this  character and loving her and so when i  felt or i perceived that the character  was not being treated with the respect  that she deserved no money in the world  would make me stay luckily for fans de  pablo wasn't done with david just yet  returning in season 17 for a  five-episode arc helping out mark  harmon's character agent gibbs and  finishing up her character's storyline  and when they called you and said hey  you want to come back what did you say i  said yes write a really nice storyline  and why not outside of ncis de pablo  gained a claim and accolades for her  performance in the feature film the 33  and though she was possibly executive  producing a television series with  weatherly it seems to have stalled her  last on-screen credits were in the 2018  short film the crossing and the 2019  indie feature film seneca with nothing  currently set for the near future check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about ncis  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

